<title>CHILE: Chile February trade surplus rises to $139.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Chile February trade surplus rises to $139.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile posted a $139.3 million trade surplus last month, compared with a $88.6 million surplus in the same month in 1996, said the Central Bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>Exports rose last month to $1.32 billion from $1.27 billion in February last year.</p>
<p>Imports remained unchanged at $1.18 billion, said the report.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
